  "mask": "three-level ANIMATED-SEA MASK the water shader reads (§4.7.17 r5, 2026-11-05): #ffffff = the organic wave-crest FIELD (dark level, render math SEA×0.70), #000000 = base SEA (untouched). The third tone — crest accents — is RENDER MATH, not an asset level: the shader mixes field texels with base water 1 OR 2 texels west toward FOAM #dff0f4 (mix 0.70; both block members, §4.8.4) — a 2px-THICK crest on every field run, which survives the §4.8 zoom-out's 2:1 nearest halving at every sample phase (1px-only crests die at the wrong parity; b804d25's wide-zoom collapse). The mix of two block members is render math — no asset hex beyond the mask pair, so the terrain-pattern exemption stands (LEDGER EXCEPTION slot A group 13 item 3 unchanged). The r1–r4 diagonal-stripe lattice was SELF-SIMILAR under translation (every 8×8 block held exactly 16 field px at every phase; translate-by-4 correlation 1.0 at (0,±4)) — the 800 ms scroll read as a static hatch. r5 replaces it with hand-authored irregular wave-crest clusters.",
